{"title":"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/72457cb47799159bbe79b8bbda486a478835b6a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> be the set of all positive real numbers. Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b730bd7ffb223c7fb1b54ba031e633b2180aed4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0} \\to \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> such that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7b5690ea082215fb2d764a73be1ae434cc3c4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y\\in \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> we have<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e9b17e39cd2c0466afbdc665b6d09a07d9a50e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = f(f(f(x)) + y) + f(xf(y)) f(x+y).\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th iteration of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa62f84d8f61b6891e92197064bf60a07467b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(n)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>First we prove that, for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf32406671fc9a01b1982019404e3f981a0f56b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed60579fa752b3762684c5a339599c4aa8fe1145.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\leq f(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/3299424bf9fa91689f9afded1a8bcc3295cf2eae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)\\geq y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"23\" />. (1)\n</p><p>Otherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8ade73a5bf2bd3248493ec470dcbcd0c7a70f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;f^{(2)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"23\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13da4cf1909b80d063b564019131370d05085264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-f^{(2)}(x)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"23\" />; we call this value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1bb51afff5fb240f36891f4551733ba8a674630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, we can substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> in the equation given in the problem, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56533b7cbe4984c3d99962454ae071f023aadc22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=f(f(f(x))+c)+f(xf(c))f(x+c)\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" /> Recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b719be2184b1cc6d0828dfd1d5e5c882bde343a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=y-f^{(2)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"23\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da3ab9d30d4da2d4c030e5d1e62b14cde70e0a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(x))+c=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />; so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30fffd756c2e17964a76ed07e98e440e1f52146d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(y)+f(xf(c))f(x+c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"20\" />. However, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is defined on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262f7340b576599ffb4964a0b2b3079c6241b43b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3a8ff31de87e09df8cfa85fb1809140fb2ae88f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xf(c))&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c2e7b65d8002c82f9c0fe830a42d9718cb9304.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+c)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />; so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699b9dd71b974558c59c1894a50ce4a715725e75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xf(c))f(x+c)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61fcc9bb5ddb258e760207ac2140e2d8ed6a3fb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(y)+f(xf(c))f(x+c)&gt;f(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"311\" height=\"20\" />, which is a contradiction.\n</p><p><br />\nNow, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7cf82e04dcc02a615e6dc6f66adca7f4d1e5e30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\leq f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314c9d0bfe92b8d936eac96172f7c0d93a1e4588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)\\geq x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"23\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a690804b3072b18c9c016feceea1b3e77d624bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(4)}(x)=f^{(2)}(f^{(2)}(x))\\geq f^{(2)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Also, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d6366890e49010e0565bbd1ddf20e878bd55fd6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(3)}(x)=f^{(2)}(f(x))\\geq f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"23\" />, and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad915f2e46272d9de4936a3556b72a54ecf7af2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(5)}(x)=f^{(2)}(f^{(3)}(x)) \\geq f^{(3)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a3f5524f163eaff7c2f969b5f67a9b823b392a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\leq f^{(5)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"23\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d3cb9c5441a22c123a90270f6368c575c70187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)\\leq f(f^{(4)}(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" />; from (1) we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/0769e8e6e99e3b1664657686e6c7d5e80781435f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)\\geq f^{(4)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/0769e8e6e99e3b1664657686e6c7d5e80781435f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)\\geq f^{(4)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />, while we also obtained <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d0367c2b51290f636ec384e69012f4bdbf320471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(4)}(x)\\geq f^{(2)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a868f808adef625bffb5a81951de0e89836bf714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)=f^{(4)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Then we try to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is injective.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is not injective, this means there exists some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710e3e4f18d7c0270ab719a00adc61fa12363b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a3e8af5f33424ae76a84b41c09c1bfdda1b046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>First consider substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f717ea27d1209b79da2c7c0a411137027ebc3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, hence we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd0973867f8d8c06ecc85170f3cdfdf79ad4c383.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(f^{(2)}(x))=f(f(f(f^{(2)}(x)))+a)+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(a))f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"21\" /> which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7aae7c1a840791c3247896aa207856a48e99407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(3)}(x)=f(f^{(4)}(x)+a)+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(a))f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(a))f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"814\" height=\"23\" />, and that obtains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3f11e8aa7ee60aa763e3c151d89c39bf3773f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(3)}(x)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)(1+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(a)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"348\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Symmetrically, if we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f717ea27d1209b79da2c7c0a411137027ebc3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, we shall obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f453a20365cad4002bbd84f4b56e8c7ff51b6e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(3)}(x)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+b)(1+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(b)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"344\" height=\"23\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99c4eea035ce43d628ef43568fc8d923f76565f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)(1+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(a)))=f(f^{(2)}(x)+b)(1+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(b)))\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>However, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a3e8af5f33424ae76a84b41c09c1bfdda1b046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef2fe33862d510aa5f4098aec09174402cf2f02d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(a)))=(1+f(f^{(2)}(x)f(b)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"341\" height=\"23\" />; then we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed8e759507461881e8f4172b316a0c8ccd1dd7cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+b).\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Now we substitute only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/9397a29eba55ae040487bd85acc87623e1ba4a04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=f(f(f(x))+a)+f(x(f(a))f(x+a)\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"18\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/b/c2bc6059ca1903815385a7a30aba8a9794e7058b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)+f(x(f(a))f(x+a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"338\" height=\"23\" />. Symmetrically substituting only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d0673589d682e091012aceece8bcac10edfcb18c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+b)+f(x(f(b))f(x+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"333\" height=\"23\" />, so finally\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17c1d06114bd1f346259e1daaef04a9eb5530af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)+f(x(f(a))f(x+a)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+b)+f(x(f(b))f(x+b)\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>But we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/414986951578d0ec818a59fcd66cd7f44b84996e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f^{(2)}(x)+a)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"244\" height=\"23\" />, and as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a3e8af5f33424ae76a84b41c09c1bfdda1b046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa7d57142fe5fc3af436f3763136e21ad924ac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x(f(a))=f(xf(b))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />, so finally we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/167d4ce670f89f6b6fdc066a5a00f6ddc223787e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+a)=f(x+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a periodic function with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c60c151331e235dc6d9df7ca403b6f0c9af39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> as a period. We can always take an arbitrarily large integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/f/0efe71c940db966f7dfa6067967c372636c9aa45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(a)&lt;a+n(b-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Recall the statement of (1), whose contrapositive is \"if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c1ec51c134a5207b6dd5e32c107b7d900c9eca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)&lt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"23\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65b3f5f6e376c2dffa249d1fe668af207f5880b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)&gt;f(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />\". By comparing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/f/0efe71c940db966f7dfa6067967c372636c9aa45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(a)&lt;a+n(b-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"23\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f1c4cc968ab9bf4f4050cac8e2346cd88a08db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)&gt;f(a+n(b-a))=f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"241\" height=\"20\" />, which is a contradiction!\n</p><p>Hence, we finished the proof that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is injective.\n</p><p>Then,as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/003ba1f57aa776e0ad2fc3b71bad86f5f35ab982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(4)}(x)=f^{(2)}(f^{(2)}(x))=f^{(2)}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"23\" />, we can conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076c60d45185d30a00baa570b27e2fce897e4222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{(2)}(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Recall the original equation, which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c7626a87ff7397a0382c145eaf89a603a326e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(f(f(x))+y)+f(xf(y))f(x+y)=f(f^{(2)}(x)+y)+f(xf(y))f(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"632\" height=\"23\" />, and it further means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/678483a52d97816558c99b30e727d531568f0b82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=f(x+y)+f(xf(y))f(x+y)\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/584110d3edbfce738fbf07574bf01f60b4ac7b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=f(1+y)+f(1\\cdot f(y))f(1+y)=f(1+y)+f(f(y))f(1+y)=f(1+y)+yf(1+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"722\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf852307c305147f2ddb7ac25f49325e5c61fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=f(1+y)(1+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e817d45b539da8388241d1f18ecb745a57dff1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1+y)=\\frac{f(1)}{1+y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"137\" height=\"44\" />. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5b19bf7575fdc3655bb5767980f09dbb747a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> as d, so we have proved that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d6952144f1afe353ee4802ef7be9f56a2d0aebb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1+y&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />, it is true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f5e439623d5a82dc9656379a985f789df544b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)=\\frac{d}{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/0/6401b860c9036becbc3755a2d0a50d72176690db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301469a1d6b6bd4ddb15b26b27e22c03d5611b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a139c53305ec3bcacb20a026e54d50e48fdc9096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(x+f(z))+f(xf(f(z)))f(x+f(z))=f(x+f(z))+f(xz)f(x+f(z))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"637\" height=\"20\" />. As the choice for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is arbitrary, we can always take some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f4b7072895063c93ccbf87b0b5c9964bb929c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;\\frac{1}{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/0/6401b860c9036becbc3755a2d0a50d72176690db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56cbba81dd1033cee4b282baac3533529ddc20d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz&gt;\\frac{1}{z}\\cdot z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />. So for the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b1ee6d72d6fe682303a60d45d14913e595a12f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=f(x+f(z))+f(xz)f(x+f(z))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"312\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e36587c3585200cd6f2bcf87259193c6ce027d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+f(z)&gt;x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd9381c71e045e810d9bcc568cb8efc03e76479d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xz&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />. Then we can write \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b58c13864859be02516a27d2bdef4e2a7c12dc1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{d}{x}=\\frac{d}{x+f(z)}+\\frac{d}{xz}\\cdot\\frac{d}{x+f(z)}\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fbc60dae41d32bf70b03021b2a6ebdcebaf803f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xz(x+f(z))}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"40\" /> on both sides give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcf51bbab305a90041ad42066f58d2f017155297.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z(x+f(z))=xz+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f5e439623d5a82dc9656379a985f789df544b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)=\\frac{d}{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>We have finally proved that, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, it is true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f5e439623d5a82dc9656379a985f789df544b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(z)=\\frac{d}{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />; and we thus conclude our final answer, that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca658cb7f1377df5f2269e2f8ddda20aac5b70b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{f(x)=\\frac{d}{x}}\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"49\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2a7adab67c1b51d8cf7a98d7ad324265690742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\in\\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>~数之谜\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO\" title=\"2022 USAMO\">2022 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2022\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022346\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.068 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 603/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 21080/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.752      1 -total\n 56.46%    6.635      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 41.00%    4.818      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22673:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022346 and revision id 279845. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}